[size=5]CraftFromChests[/size]

Craft, upgrade and build using the items inside nearby chests. No more hauling
stacks of wood and iron into your inventory before every crafting session.

[size=4]What it does[/size]
[list]
[*]The recipe list, the have/need numbers and the craft button all count the contents of nearby chests.
[*]Hammer, hoe and cultivator building costs are paid from those chests too, and that part can be turned off.
[*]Items in your own inventory are always spent first, then the chests, closest one first.
[/list]

[size=4]Which chests count[/size]
A chest is only used if it passes the same rules the game applies when you try to open it: inside the configured radius, public or created by you, guard stone access when the chest checks for one, and nobody else has it open right now.

[size=4]Multiplayer[/size]
This is a client side mod. Only the player using it needs it installed, and it works on a vanilla dedicated server with no server side component. Before taking an item the mod claims network ownership of the chest, which is the same mechanism the game uses for "take all". Players without the mod are unaffected.

[size=4]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*]Valheim 1.0.7
[*]BepInEx 5 for Valheim, the denikson BepInExPack_Valheim pack
[/list]

[size=4]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install BepInEx 5 for Valheim and run the game once.
[*]Extract this archive into the Valheim folder, so the dll ends up in BepInEx\plugins\CraftFromChests\.
[*]Start the game. BepInEx\LogOutput.log should contain a line reading CraftFromChests loaded.
[/list]

With r2modman or Thunderstore Mod Manager, use Import local mod and pick the Thunderstore flavoured zip instead.

[size=4]Configuration[/size]
Edit BepInEx\config\dev.trentini.craftfromchests.cfg with the game closed.
[list]
[*]Range, default 20 meters
[*]UseForBuilding, default true
[*]IncludeVehicleContainers, default true, covers carts and ships
[*]Enabled, master switch
[/list]

